#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bed4e59-ea2f-5060-9beb-e52473607292" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c28204d-80b4-5bff-b6e8-3477b92e218b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y-z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364732} {:answer/id #uuid "717424c2-ec13-5ac7-875e-88621ff7bdaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-y-6z=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364733} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8df72d-3c04-5e05-8795-e4c6fbaba38f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x-2y-7z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364734} {:answer/id #uuid "95f9c3db-4482-5ce3-9b21-2d58e2f41fb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x-y+2z=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364735} {:answer/id #uuid "da7a8a85-618c-5fdd-9471-3999ed61c8aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-8y+3z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b8df72d-3c04-5e05-8795-e4c6fbaba38f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x-2y-7z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364734} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f2058d6-9b0c-565a-9822-120458ac4d00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18388a52-c34d-5096-91df-d66aad50a515" :question/math-academy-id "q-109713" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2u+v,\\,{v}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,uv⟩$ at the point where $u=0$ and $v=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=0$ and $v=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(0,2) & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(0,2) & =⟨1,\\,2(2),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(0,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(0,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,\\,2,\\,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=0$ and $v=2$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2(0)+2,\\,{2}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0,\\,0\\cdot 2)=(2,4,0),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-8,\\,2,\\,7⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-4,\\,z⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-8)\\cdot (x-2)+2\\cdot (y-4)+7\\cdot z & =0 \\\\ -8x+2y+7z+8 & =0 \\\\ 8x-2y-7z & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bed4e59-ea2f-5060-9beb-e52473607292" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82df2ad7-dfce-516a-afc5-73f79a7de2d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\,x-y+z=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364739} {:answer/id #uuid "43ebb03e-623b-5fed-8449-71ea7ef71758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2\\sqrt{3}\\,y=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364740} {:answer/id #uuid "1f4f946f-f58b-5cde-b99e-f6a0bd985e76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\,x+2z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364741} {:answer/id #uuid "64e05259-546b-5406-ac85-44ca3dacc2be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\sqrt{3}\\,y=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364742} {:answer/id #uuid "64ec14ca-bcd4-5d74-bb04-7c83c60313c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-\\sqrt{3}\\,y+z=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64e05259-546b-5406-ac85-44ca3dacc2be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\sqrt{3}\\,y=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364742} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc871a30-d9c4-5803-bf5d-65ce6f68cec4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b642b9a-3339-58d2-82e7-7f92410bd771" :question/math-academy-id "q-109764" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩$ at the point where $u=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{3},\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-2\\sqrt{3},\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))=(1,\\sqrt{3},0),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-2,\\,-2\\sqrt{3},\\,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-\\sqrt{3},\\,z⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot (x-1)-2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (y-\\sqrt{3})+0\\cdot z & =0 \\\\ -2x-2\\sqrt{3\\,}y+8 & =0 \\\\ -x-\\sqrt{3}\\,y+4 & =0 \\\\ x+\\sqrt{3}\\,y & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d5da71e-534c-57b6-9b55-0d85d01f1b9c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01131d65-1529-5ae4-81f9-b5674144dfb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2y+z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364746} {:answer/id #uuid "0609a39c-4b44-5efb-8bab-73594b6c5e83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y+3z=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364747} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f38947-b276-5a6b-a794-99547965e83f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-2y+z=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364748} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc0944c-0545-5ab7-b128-d2ecd63611c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-3y+z=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364749} {:answer/id #uuid "25afae6d-f4c6-56ef-83de-668fa3fd6025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y+2z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25afae6d-f4c6-56ef-83de-668fa3fd6025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y+2z=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364750} :answer-field/id #uuid "2752edb0-2174-550a-ad13-19724349ebb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364745}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa050d19-e824-5497-b452-091eb0f21397" :question/math-academy-id "q-109814" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=1-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,y=-v,\\,z=-u\n$$\n\nat the point $(-1,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨1-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,-v,\\,-u⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(-1,-1,1)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}=-1 \\\\ -v=-1 \\\\ -u=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=-1 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2v,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=-1$ and $v=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(-1,1) & =⟨-2(-1),\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(-1,1) & =⟨-2(1),\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(-1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(-1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (x+1)+2\\cdot (y+1)+(-2)\\cdot (z-1) & =0 \\\\ -x+2y-2z+3 & =0 \\\\ x-2y+2z & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d5da71e-534c-57b6-9b55-0d85d01f1b9c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edd6c28c-0742-5875-81ea-2f505d875e95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2y-6z=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364753} {:answer/id #uuid "2fb5265a-341d-5a03-8d45-bce93ca0eb73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-y-3z=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364754} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd3e616-2ed3-5539-ae69-9638a9b54143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y-6z=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364755} {:answer/id #uuid "5b879075-03c9-59ce-ae50-ce08a3477e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2y+12z=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364756} {:answer/id #uuid "d83fc19b-c98b-5abb-bf4f-378778bb589b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y-4z=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b879075-03c9-59ce-ae50-ce08a3477e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-2y+12z=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364756} :answer-field/id #uuid "c547d5a2-ab92-505f-b038-d71b5b261dfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364752}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d8fdb53f-d745-5c44-8e1d-90e2caddd152" :question/math-academy-id "q-109824" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n\n$$\nx=2{u}^{3},\\,y=u{v}^{2},\\,z=v\n$$\n\nat the point $(2,9,3).$" :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2{u}^{3},\\,u{v}^{2},\\,v⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(2,9,3)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{u}^{3}=2 \\\\ u{v}^{2}=9 \\\\ v=3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2{u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2{u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2uv,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,3) & =⟨6(1)^{2},\\,{3}^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,9,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,3) & =⟨0,\\,2(1)(3),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,6,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,3)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,3) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 6 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,\\,-6,\\,36⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨9,\\,-6,\\,36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-9,\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ 9\\cdot (x-2)+(-6)\\cdot (y-9)+36\\cdot (z-3) & =0 \\\\ 9x-6y+36z-72 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+12z & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364758 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bb08b6-6e41-51e9-853f-cd28a5c35a2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29789cfc-ae47-50d3-9eef-de4ebbf78fbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,0,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364760} {:answer/id #uuid "d724b8ce-15df-54ea-83df-b35705131d14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364761} {:answer/id #uuid "47ed922b-193c-52e6-9d6f-28b1a44ae83a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364762} {:answer/id #uuid "b21506d6-2842-5fac-b818-7bab500b0d46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,0,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364763} {:answer/id #uuid "8c153b40-274a-57de-a620-ffedfa1876f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47ed922b-193c-52e6-9d6f-28b1a44ae83a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364762} :answer-field/id #uuid "71e2b1bb-e57e-5124-b439-5677b114d463" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb247dbf-bbf5-58ef-b635-b65ed8200697" :question/math-academy-id "q-110067" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨v,\\,1+u,\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩$ at the point $(1,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $(1,2,1)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}v=1 \\\\ 1+u=2 \\\\ {u}^{2}{v}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u=1 \\\\ v=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2u{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2{u}^{2}v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2(1)(1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2(1)^{2}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(1,1)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(1,1) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
